BGP Unnumbered relies strictly on automatically learned IPv6 Link-Local paths. We need strip all static IPv4 subnets from the interfaces
(Ethernet0, Ethernet4, etc.) so they do not override the link-local behavior and activate ipv6 such as     "INTERFACE": {
        "Ethernet0": {
            "ipv6_use_link_local_only": "enable"
        },
        "Ethernet4": {
            "ipv6_use_link_local_only": "enable"
        },
        "Ethernet8": {
            "ipv6_use_link_local_only": "enable"
        },
        "Ethernet12": {
            "ipv6_use_link_local_only": "enable"
        },
        "Ethernet16": {
            "ipv6_use_link_local_only": "enable"
        },
        "Ethernet20": {
            "ipv6_use_link_local_only": "enable"
        }
  }


